{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "ec2b4d8b-2f27-882b-ab88-2457bac0e0f4",
  "created_at": "2026-03-05T11:23:28-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Leo Cirelli",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Anita Chaudhry",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:21:09-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Anita. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:21:13-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, hello, good morning. Is it still morning? Yes, just barely. My name is Leo Cirelli, I'm over at 266 Coggeshall Avenue, up on the Hill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:21:21-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning, Mr. Cirelli. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:21:25-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, I'm having a pool put in, and somebody told me there's rules about a barrier. A fence, I suppose. I don't understand it all. My brother had a pool in Cranston back in, oh, it was the year of the big blizzard, and the whole yard was, well, never mind that. Sorry."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:21:40-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's all right. So you're putting in a pool and you'd like to know about fencing around it. Is it an in-ground pool or an above-ground one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:21:48-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "In-ground, I think. Is that the one that's dug? The fellow said in-ground. Or maybe he said inground, all one word."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:21:54-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, in-ground means dug into the yard. Do you know how tall you want the fence?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:21:59-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm planning cedar. I like the smell of it. And whatever is allowed tall, I'd go that, I don't know the number. Is it four feet? Or six? Somebody said four, but then my neighbor said six."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:22:09-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There are height requirements for pool barriers, and they can be different from a regular yard fence. The inspector can go over the exact height with you. Do you have a contractor lined up?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:22:19-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, the guy who's doing the pool, he says he'll start on the fence after. So, do I need to pull a permit before the guy starts? Is that the expression, pull a permit?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:22:29-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's the expression, yes. In general a fence does need a permit, and with a pool it's definitely something to get squared away before any work starts. You'd apply through our office, usually with a simple sketch of the yard."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:22:40-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A sketch. I'm no good at drawing. Does the guy do that, or me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:22:44-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Often the contractor can supply it. Just ask him to put the pool and fence on a plan of your lot."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:22:50-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "All right, all right. And the fee? Is there a fee? I hope it's not like a house."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:22:56-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There is a fee, but I can't quote you the amount from here. When you send in the application, the office will tell you exactly what it is. I can also mail you the form if you'd like."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:23:07-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hold on one second, my kettle is going. [pause] There, it clicked off. I'm pouring my tea. Sorry. So the permit first, and then the fee, and then the guy starts. Is that right? Or the guy first?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:23:18-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Permit first, then he starts. Would you like me to take your address for the mailing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-05T11:23:23-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I said 266 Coggeshall, didn't I? Yes. Thank you, dear. I think I've got it, mostly."
    }
  ],
